    "title": "wallet: return error from bitcoin-wallet create",
    "user": {
      "login": "kriss39",
      "id": 93033289,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBYuTSQ",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93033289?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/kriss39",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`bitcoin-wallet create` exits with status 0 even when the wallet couldn't be created:\n\n```\n$ bitcoin-wallet -regtest -wallet=w1 create   # first time, ok\n$ bitcoin-wallet -regtest -wallet=w1 create\nFailed to create database path '.../regtest/wallets/w1'. Database already exists.\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\nIn `ExecuteWalletToolFunc` the `create` branch only does something when `MakeWallet` succeeds and then falls through to `return true`. The other commands (`info`, `dump`, `createfromdump`) all return false on failure. So scripts that check the exit code think the wallet was created.\n\nThis returns false when `MakeWallet` fails, the same way `info` does. The added check in `tool_wallet.py` runs `create` on the existing wallet `foo` and expects exit code 1. It fails on master (`not(0 == 1)`) and passes with the fix.\n",
